  <node unique_id="12" master_id="0" name="2. Database Info" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="1" foreground="" ts_creation="1792703477" ts_lastsave="1792703477">
    <rich_text>Schema, constraints, SQL scripts and known mismatches.</rich_text>
    <node unique_id="7" master_id="0" name="Database Overview" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="1792703477" ts_lastsave="1792703477">
      <rich_text>DATABASE NAME : student_information_system_db
ENGINE        : MySQL 8.0 / MariaDB
TABLES        : 1 (Student)

Files:
  database/migrations/001_initial_setup.sql  - creates the database and the Student table
  database/seeds/001_sample_data.sql         - inserts two sample students

Run order: migration first, then seed.
</rich_text>
    </node>
    <node unique_id="8" master_id="0" name="Student Table - Columns" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="1792703477" ts_lastsave="1792739241">
      <rich_text>TABLE: Student

Column               Type                  Rules
----------------      --------------        ----------------------------------------------
Student_ID          VARCHAR(20)     PRIMARY KEY
Full_Name           VARCHAR(100)   NOT NULL
Gender               VARCHAR(20)     NOT NULL
Year_Level           INT                  NOT NULL, CHECK between 1 and 4
Program              VARCHAR(100)   NOT NULL
Contact_Number   VARCHAR(11)    NOT NULL, UNIQUE, CHECK regex ^[0-9]{11}$

CONSTRAINTS
  chk_contact_number : Contact_Number must be exactly 11 digits (REGEXP '^[0-9]{11}$')
  Year_Level CHECK    : value must be 1, 2, 3 or 4
  UNIQUE                  : no two students may share a contact number

C# MAPPING (Student.cs)
  Student_ID        -&gt; StudentId
  Full_Name         -&gt; FullName
  Gender             -&gt; Gender
  Year_Level         -&gt; YearLevel
  Program            -&gt; Program
  Contact_Number -&gt; ContactNumber
</rich_text>
    </node>
    <node unique_id="9" master_id="0" name="SQL - Schema (001_initial_setup.sql)" prog_lang="sql" tags="" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="1792703477" ts_lastsave="1792703477">
      <rich_text>CREATE DATABASE IF NOT EXISTS student_information_system_db;

USE student_information_system_db;

CREATE TABLE Student (
    Student_ID VARCHAR(20) PRIMARY KEY,
    Full_Name VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL,
    Gender VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL,
    Year_Level INT NOT NULL CHECK (Year_Level BETWEEN 1 AND 4),
    Program VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL,
    Contact_Number VARCHAR(11) NOT NULL UNIQUE,

    CONSTRAINT chk_contact_number
        CHECK (Contact_Number REGEXP '^[0-9]{11}$')
);</rich_text>
    </node>
    <node unique_id="10" master_id="0" name="SQL - Seed Data (001_sample_data.sql)" prog_lang="sql" tags="" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="1792703477" ts_lastsave="1792703477">
      <rich_text>USE student_information_system_db;

INSERT INTO Student (
    Student_ID,
    Full_Name,
    Gender,
    Year_Level,
    Program,
    Contact_Number
)
VALUES 
    ('2024-001', 'Juan Dela Cruz', 'Male', 2, 'BS Computer Science', '09935382981'),
    ('2024-002', 'Maria Clara Santos', 'Female', 2, 'BS Information Technology', '09662143078')
ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE
    Full_Name = VALUES(Full_Name);</rich_text>
    </node>
    <node unique_id="11" master_id="0" name="Database Notes &amp; Known Mismatches" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="1792703477" ts_lastsave="1792737694">
      <rich_text>1) The form allows Year Level 1 to 8, but the database CHECK only allows 1 to 4. Entering 5 to 8 will pass the form validation and then fail in MySQL.
   Fix: change the form to 1-4, or change the CHECK to BETWEEN 1 AND 8.

2) StudentRepository tries these table names in order: Student, students, student, student_information, student_information_system. The schema only uses Student, so the guessing is unnecessary.

3) The seed uses ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE Full_Name = VALUES(Full_Name), so it can be re-run safely.
</rich_text>
    </node>
  </node>
  <node unique_id="20" master_id="0" name="3. Setup Guide" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="1" foreground="" ts_creation="1792703477" ts_lastsave="1792703477">
    <rich_text>Environment setup, dependencies, configuration and troubleshooting.</rich_text>
    <node unique_id="13" master_id="0" name="Prerequisites" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="1792703477" ts_lastsave="1792703477">
      <rich_text>REQUIRED
  - Windows 10 (1903+) or Windows 11, 64-bit
  - Visual Studio 2022 (latest) with the ".NET desktop development" workload
  - .NET 10 SDK (the project targets net10.0-windows)
  - MySQL Server 8.0 or XAMPP (MariaDB)
  - Git

NOT RECOMMENDED
  Windows 7, 8 and 8.1: TLS 1.2 problems with the MySQL driver, high-DPI scaling glitches, and missing runtime updates.
</rich_text>
    </node>
    <node unique_id="14" master_id="0" name="Step 1 - Database" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="1792703477" ts_lastsave="1792703477">
      <rich_text>1. Start MySQL (XAMPP Control Panel &gt; Start MySQL, or MySQL Workbench).
2. Open a SQL client (phpMyAdmin, MySQL Workbench, or the mysql command line).
3. Run database/migrations/001_initial_setup.sql
   This creates student_information_system_db and the Student table.
4. Run database/seeds/001_sample_data.sql
   This inserts two sample students.

COMMAND LINE EXAMPLE
  mysql -u root -p &lt; database/migrations/001_initial_setup.sql
  mysql -u root -p &lt; database/seeds/001_sample_data.sql
</rich_text>
    </node>
    <node unique_id="15" master_id="0" name="Step 2 - Clone &amp; Open" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="1792703477" ts_lastsave="1792703477">
      <rich_text>  git clone https://github.com/gabaga1926/Student-Information-System.git
  cd Student-Information-System

Open Interface/Interface.slnx in Visual Studio.
Let NuGet restore the packages (MySql.Data and Microsoft.Extensions.Configuration.Json).
</rich_text>
    </node>
    <node unique_id="16" master_id="0" name="Step 3 - appsettings.json (example)" prog_lang="json" tags="" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="1792703477" ts_lastsave="1792735820">
      <rich_text>{
  "ConnectionStrings": {
    "StudentDb": "Server=localhost;Port=3306;Database=student_information_system_db;Uid=root;Pwd=YOUR_PASSWORD;charset=utf8mb4;"
  }
}
</rich_text>
    </node>
    <node unique_id="17" master_id="0" name="Step 3 - appsettings.json notes" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="1792703477" ts_lastsave="1792703477">
      <rich_text>WHY YOU NEED THIS FILE
The repo does not include appsettings.json (it is in .gitignore so passwords are not committed). Without it, the app shows "appsettings.json was not found".

WHERE TO PUT IT
StudentRepository.GetConnectionString() starts in the app's output folder and walks UP through parent folders until it finds appsettings.json. Putting it in the Interface/ project folder works.

IMPORTANT
  - The key name must be exactly: ConnectionStrings &gt; StudentDb
  - The example JSON in the next node was written for this documentation. It is not a file from the repo.
  - If you want it copied to the output folder automatically, set "Copy to Output Directory" to "Copy if newer" in the file's Properties in Visual Studio. Not required because of the parent-folder search.
  - Never commit your real password.
</rich_text>
    </node>
    <node unique_id="18" master_id="0" name="Step 4 - Run" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="1792703477" ts_lastsave="1792703477">
      <rich_text>Press F5 in Visual Studio (or run: dotnet run --project Interface).
On start, Form1_Load calls StudentRepository.EnsureSchema() and then LoadStudents().
If the connection fails, a "Database Error" message box shows the exception message.
</rich_text>
    </node>
    <node unique_id="19" master_id="0" name="Troubleshooting" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="1792703477" ts_lastsave="1792703477">
      <rich_text>"appsettings.json was not found"
  Create the file (see Step 3) in the Interface folder.

"Connection string 'StudentDb' was not found in appsettings.json"
  The key must be ConnectionStrings:StudentDb.

"Unable to connect to any of the specified MySQL hosts"
  MySQL is not running, wrong port, or wrong credentials. Start MySQL and check the connection string.

"Unknown database 'student_information_system_db'"
  Run the migration script first.

"No student table was found in the configured database"
  The Database= in your connection string points to the wrong database, or the migration was not run.

Add/Update fails with a CHECK constraint error
  Year level must be 1-4 and contact number must be 11 digits in the database.

Duplicate entry for key 'Contact_Number' or 'PRIMARY'
  Student ID and contact number must both be unique.

Build errors about net10.0
  Install the .NET 10 SDK and update Visual Studio.
</rich_text>
    </node>
  </node>
  <node unique_id="32" master_id="0" name="4. App Walkthrough" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="1" foreground="" ts_creation="1792703477" ts_lastsave="1792739098">
