    <node unique_id="22" master_id="0" name="Startup &amp; Load" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="1792703477" ts_lastsave="1792739747">
      <rich_text>FLOW
  Program.Main -&gt; ApplicationConfiguration.Initialize() -&gt; Application.Run(new Form1())
  Form1 constructor: InitializeComponent(), then attaches Load, btnClear.Click, btnUpdate.Click, btnDelete.Click handlers.
  (btnAdd is wired inside Form1.Designer.cs to button1_Click.)

Form1_Load
  1. StudentRepository.EnsureSchema()  - confirms a student table exists
  2. LoadStudents()                            - fills dgvStudents from the database
  3. ClearForm()                                - empties the inputs

Any exception shows a "Database Error" MessageBox.
</rich_text>
    </node>
    <node unique_id="23" master_id="0" name="Feature - Add Student" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="1792703477" ts_lastsave="1792703477">
      <rich_text>Handler: button1_Click (wired to btnAdd in the designer)

STEPS
  1. BuildStudentFromForm() validates the inputs. If invalid, a warning is shown and nothing happens.
  2. StudentRepository.AddStudent(student) runs a parameterized INSERT.
  3. Success MessageBox, then LoadStudents() refreshes the grid and ClearForm() resets the inputs.

ERRORS
  MySqlException -&gt; "Database error while adding the student."
  Any other exception -&gt; "Unable to add student."
  (Duplicate Student ID or contact number comes back as a MySqlException.)
</rich_text>
    </node>
    <node unique_id="24" master_id="0" name="Feature - Update Student" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="1792703477" ts_lastsave="1792703477">
      <rich_text>Handler: btnUpdate_Click

STEPS
  1. Click a grid row (or type an existing Student ID) so the form holds the record.
  2. Edit the fields. The Student ID is the lookup key and is not changed.
  3. Click Update. BuildStudentFromForm() validates, then UpdateStudent() runs UPDATE ... WHERE Student_ID = @Student_ID.
  4. If 0 rows are affected, it throws "Student ID was not found for update."

On success: message box, grid refresh, form cleared.
</rich_text>
    </node>
    <node unique_id="25" master_id="0" name="Feature - Delete Student" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="1792703477" ts_lastsave="1792703477">
      <rich_text>Handler: btnDelete_Click

STEPS
  1. Needs a Student ID in the form (select a row or type one). Otherwise: "Select a student or enter a Student ID to delete."
  2. Confirmation dialog: "Delete student '&lt;id&gt;'?" (Yes / No, warning icon). No cancels.
  3. StudentRepository.DeleteStudent(id) runs DELETE ... WHERE Student_ID = @Student_ID.
  4. If 0 rows are affected, it throws "Student ID was not found for deletion."

On success: message box, grid refresh, form cleared.
</rich_text>
    </node>
    <node unique_id="26" master_id="0" name="Feature - Clear Form" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="1792703477" ts_lastsave="1792703477">
      <rich_text>Handler: btnClear_Click -&gt; ClearForm()

Clears txtStudentId, txtFullName, txtYearLevel, txtProgram, txtContactNumber, resets cboGender to no selection (-1), clears the grid selection and puts focus back in txtStudentId.
</rich_text>
    </node>
    <node unique_id="40" master_id="0" name="Feature - Button States" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="1792738860" ts_lastsave="1792739422">
      <rich_text weight="heavy">Button States (ADD / UPDATE / DELETE / CLEAR)</rich_text>
      <rich_text>

The four action buttons enable or disable automatically based on whether an entry is selected in the list. This prevents invalid actions, such as updating a record that doesn’t exist yet or adding a duplicate of one already loaded.

Use this state to start a new record. Fill in the fields and click ADD to save it.
</rich_text>
      <rich_text weight="heavy">State 1: No entry selected, fields empty</rich_text>
      <rich_text>
• ADD: enabled
• CLEAR: enabled
• UPDATE: grayed out
• DELETE: grayed out

You have typed data, but it hasn’t been saved yet. Click ADD to save it as a new entry, or CLEAR to discard what you typed.
</rich_text>
      <rich_text weight="heavy">State 2: No entry selected, fields filled</rich_text>
      <rich_text>
• ADD: enabled
• CLEAR: enabled
• UPDATE: grayed out
• DELETE: grayed out

The selected entry’s data loads into the fields. Edit them and click UPDATE to save changes, or click DELETE to remove the entry. ADD and CLEAR are disabled so you can’t accidentally create a duplicate or wipe the loaded record.
</rich_text>
      <rich_text weight="heavy">State 3: Entry selected</rich_text>
      <rich_text>
• ADD: grayed out
• CLEAR: grayed out
• UPDATE: enabled
• DELETE: enabled

</rich_text>
      <rich_text weight="heavy">Quick Reference Table</rich_text>
      <rich_text>
</rich_text>
      <rich_text justification="left"></rich_text>
      <rich_text>

</rich_text>
      <rich_text weight="heavy">Notes</rich_text>
      <rich_text>
- To return to State 1 or 2 from State 3, deselect the entry in the list.
- The buttons depend only on selection, not on field content. Whether the fields are empty or filled makes no difference when nothing is selected.
- If a button is grayed out, check the selection state first, since that is the most common reason.

</rich_text>
